00:04:15,652 --> 00:04:21,652
Get some action.

2
00:08:31,304 --> 00:08:37,304
Charlie's Angels is a action, comedy, adventure film directed by McG.

3
00:12:46,956 --> 00:12:52,956
The captivating crime-fighting trio who are masters of
disguise, espionage and martial arts are back!

4
00:17:02,608 --> 00:17:08,608
When a devious mastermind embroils them in a plot to destroy individual privacy, the Angels,
aided by their loyal sidekick Bosley, set out to bring down the bad guys.

5
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:24,260
But when a terrible secret is revealed, it makes the
Angels targets for assassination.

6
00:25:33,913 --> 00:25:39,913
Natalie Cook, played by Cameron Diaz.

7
00:29:49,565 --> 00:29:55,565
Dylan Sanders, played by Drew Barrymore.

8
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Alex Munday, played by Lucy Liu.

9
00:38:20,869 --> 00:38:26,869
John Bosley, played by Bill Murray.

10
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:42,521
Eric Knox, played by Sam Rockwell.

11
00:46:52,173 --> 00:46:58,173
Roger Corwin, played by Tim Curry.

12
00:51:07,826 --> 00:51:13,826
Charlie's Angels is a 2000 American spy action comedy film directed by McG in his feature
film directorial debut, and written by Ryan Rowe, Ed Solomon, and John August.

13
00:55:23,478 --> 00:55:29,478
It is the first film in the Charlie's Angels trilogy, a continuation of the
television series of the same name created by Ivan Goff and Ben Roberts.

14
00:59:39,130 --> 00:59:45,130
Unlike the original series, the film features more comic elements.

15
01:03:54,782 --> 01:04:00,782
The movie stars Cameron Diaz, Drew Barrymore, and Lucy Liu as three
women working in a private detective agency in Los Angeles.

16
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
John Forsythe reprised his role as the unseen
Charlie's voice from the original series.

17
01:12:26,086 --> 01:12:32,086
Bill Murray also stars as John Bosley, replacing David Doyle,
who played the role in the original series.

18
01:16:41,739 --> 01:16:47,739
It also stars Sam Rockwell, Tim Curry and Kelly Lynch while Crispin Glover, Matt
LeBlanc, Luke Wilson and Tom Green appear in supporting roles.

19
01:20:57,391 --> 01:21:03,391
The film was released on November 3, 2000, in the United States by Sony Pictures Releasing
under its Columbia Pictures label, and grossed $264.1 million worldwide.

20
01:25:13,043 --> 01:25:19,043
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

21
01:29:28,695 --> 01:29:34,695
The film explores themes of martial arts, undercover
agent, spy, secret agent, satire.

22
01:33:44,347 --> 01:33:50,347
The tone is lighthearted and intense.
